  "prompt": "You are writing the control policy for a peg-in-hole insertion cell.\n\nA UR5e arm holds a square peg (20 x 20 mm, 80 mm long) pointing straight down. A block on the table\nhas a square hole (21 x 21 mm, 0.5 mm clearance per side, 50 mm deep); its top surface is at z = 0.05 m.\nIn our test cell the hole is placed at x = 0.45 +/- 0.05 m, y = 0.00 +/- 0.05 m, yaw = 0 +/- 15 degrees.\nThe trial succeeds when the peg is seated at least 30 mm deep in the hole with less than 1 mm lateral error.\n\nWrite a Python module that defines `def run(api):`. It is called once per trial and must return when\nfinished. `api` is the module below; use only these four functions (plus `math`, which you may import).\nYou have at most 300 API calls per trial. Contact force above 150 N aborts the trial as a collision.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"The four functions a policy may call. A policy is `def run(api): ...` and receives this module.\n\nUnits: metres and degrees in the world frame; z is up and the table top is z = 0.\nThe robot holds a 20 x 20 mm square peg, 80 mm long, pointing straight down. The peg tip is the\ncontrolled point. The hole is a 21 x 21 mm square, 50 mm deep, cut into the top of a 50 mm-high block.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\n_SIM = None  # set by the trial runner\n\n\ndef hole_pose():\n    \"\"\"Camera estimate of the hole: returns ((x, y, z_top_surface), yaw_deg).\n    Yaw is the rotation of the square hole about z, reported in [-45, 45) because a square repeats every 90 degrees.\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.hole_pose()\n\n\ndef move_to(xyz, yaw_deg):\n    \"\"\"Move the peg tip to xyz (metres) with the peg rotated yaw_deg about z, peg pointing down.\n    Joint-space motion; blocks until the arm has settled. Moving into the block is a collision.\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.move_to(xyz, yaw_deg)\n\n\ndef step_down(mm):\n    \"\"\"Lower the peg tip by mm millimetres from the last commanded target (negative values raise it).\n    Returns the contact force on the peg in newtons after the motion settles.\n    The run is aborted as a collision if the contact force ever exceeds 150 N.\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.step_down(mm)\n\n\ndef done():\n    \"\"\"True if the peg tip is at least 30 mm below the block's top surface (i.e. seated in the hole).\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.done()\n\n```\n\nReply with the complete module in a single ```python code block, followed by at most three sentences\nexplaining the strategy.",
  "response": "```python\nimport math\n\nMAX_CALLS = 300\n\n\ndef run(api):\n    calls = [0]\n\n    def call(fn, *args):\n        calls[0] += 1\n        return fn(*args)\n\n    def left():\n        return MAX_CALLS - calls[0]\n\n    # 1. Average several camera readings. Yaw uses a circular mean on 4*yaw (square symmetry).\n    n_meas = 5\n    sx = sy = sz = 0.0\n    sc = ss = 0.0\n    for _ in range(n_meas):\n        (x, y, z), yaw = call(api.hole_pose)\n        sx += x\n        sy += y\n        sz += z\n        sc += math.cos(math.radians(4.0 * yaw))\n        ss += math.sin(math.radians(4.0 * yaw))\n    hx, hy, hz = sx / n_meas, sy / n_meas, sz / n_meas\n    hyaw = math.degrees(math.atan2(ss, sc)) / 4.0\n\n    HOVER = 0.0015      # m above top surface for each probe\n    PROBE = 2.0         # mm step: ends 0.5 mm below the surface\n    CONTACT_N = 15.0    # force meaning \"landed on the surface / edge\"\n    JAM_N = 60.0        # force meaning \"jammed while inserting\"\n    TARGET_DEPTH = 33.0 # mm below the top surface\n    INSERT_STEP = 4.0   # mm per insertion step\n\n    # 2. Search candidates: xy spiral (0.4 mm grid) sorted by radius, then small yaw offsets.\n    pitch = 0.0004\n    pts = []\n    n = 8\n    for i in range(-n, n + 1):\n        for j in range(-n, n + 1):\n            r = math.hypot(i, j) * pitch\n            if r <= n * pitch + 1e-9:\n                pts.append((r, i * pitch, j * pitch))\n    pts.sort(key=lambda p: (round(p[0], 6), math.atan2(p[2], p[1])))\n    cands = [(dx, dy, 0.0) for _, dx, dy in pts]\n    for dyaw in (1.5, -1.5, 3.0, -3.0):\n        for r, dx, dy in pts:\n            if r <= 0.0008 + 1e-9:\n                cands.append((dx, dy, dyaw))\n\n    def try_insert(px, py, pyaw):\n        \"\"\"Returns True on success. Leaves the peg at the hover height on failure.\"\"\"\n        call(api.move_to, (px, py, hz + HOVER), pyaw)\n        f = call(api.step_down, PROBE)\n        if f > CONTACT_N:\n            call(api.step_down, -PROBE)  # lift off before moving sideways\n            return False\n        depth = PROBE - HOVER * 1000.0   # mm below the top surface\n        while depth < TARGET_DEPTH:\n            if left() < 3:\n                return bool(call(api.done)) if left() > 0 else False\n            step = min(INSERT_STEP, TARGET_DEPTH - depth)\n            f = call(api.step_down, step)\n            depth += step\n            if f > JAM_N:\n                # Jammed: back off, then pull completely out and give up on this candidate.\n                call(api.step_down, -(depth + HOVER * 1000.0))\n                return False\n        if call(api.done):\n            return True\n        # Not reported seated: push slightly further once.\n        if left() >= 2:\n            f = call(api.step_down, 2.0)\n            if f <= JAM_N and call(api.done):\n                return True\n        return False\n\n    for dx, dy, dyaw in cands:\n        # need: move + probe + retract, or move + probe + ~9 insertion steps + done\n        if left() < 14:\n            break\n        if try_insert(hx + dx, hy + dy, hyaw + dyaw):\n            return\n    return\n```\n\nThe policy averages several camera readings, using a circular mean on 4\u00d7yaw because of the square's symmetry. It then probes candidate positions in a 0.4 mm spiral grid around the estimate, and later at small yaw offsets, by lowering the peg 0.5 mm below the block surface. A low contact force at that depth means the peg is inside the 0.5 mm clearance, so it is pushed down in 4 mm steps to 33 mm. A high force means the peg landed on the surface or jammed, so it lifts off before moving to the next candidate, and the loop stays within the 300-call budget and well below the 150 N abort limit.",
  "code": "import math\n\nMAX_CALLS = 300\n\n\ndef run(api):\n    calls = [0]\n\n    def call(fn, *args):\n        calls[0] += 1\n        return fn(*args)\n\n    def left():\n        return MAX_CALLS - calls[0]\n\n    # 1. Average several camera readings. Yaw uses a circular mean on 4*yaw (square symmetry).\n    n_meas = 5\n    sx = sy = sz = 0.0\n    sc = ss = 0.0\n    for _ in range(n_meas):\n        (x, y, z), yaw = call(api.hole_pose)\n        sx += x\n        sy += y\n        sz += z\n        sc += math.cos(math.radians(4.0 * yaw))\n        ss += math.sin(math.radians(4.0 * yaw))\n    hx, hy, hz = sx / n_meas, sy / n_meas, sz / n_meas\n    hyaw = math.degrees(math.atan2(ss, sc)) / 4.0\n\n    HOVER = 0.0015      # m above top surface for each probe\n    PROBE = 2.0         # mm step: ends 0.5 mm below the surface\n    CONTACT_N = 15.0    # force meaning \"landed on the surface / edge\"\n    JAM_N = 60.0        # force meaning \"jammed while inserting\"\n    TARGET_DEPTH = 33.0 # mm below the top surface\n    INSERT_STEP = 4.0   # mm per insertion step\n\n    # 2. Search candidates: xy spiral (0.4 mm grid) sorted by radius, then small yaw offsets.\n    pitch = 0.0004\n    pts = []\n    n = 8\n    for i in range(-n, n + 1):\n        for j in range(-n, n + 1):\n            r = math.hypot(i, j) * pitch\n            if r <= n * pitch + 1e-9:\n                pts.append((r, i * pitch, j * pitch))\n    pts.sort(key=lambda p: (round(p[0], 6), math.atan2(p[2], p[1])))\n    cands = [(dx, dy, 0.0) for _, dx, dy in pts]\n    for dyaw in (1.5, -1.5, 3.0, -3.0):\n        for r, dx, dy in pts:\n            if r <= 0.0008 + 1e-9:\n                cands.append((dx, dy, dyaw))\n\n    def try_insert(px, py, pyaw):\n        \"\"\"Returns True on success. Leaves the peg at the hover height on failure.\"\"\"\n        call(api.move_to, (px, py, hz + HOVER), pyaw)\n        f = call(api.step_down, PROBE)\n        if f > CONTACT_N:\n            call(api.step_down, -PROBE)  # lift off before moving sideways\n            return False\n        depth = PROBE - HOVER * 1000.0   # mm below the top surface\n        while depth < TARGET_DEPTH:\n            if left() < 3:\n                return bool(call(api.done)) if left() > 0 else False\n            step = min(INSERT_STEP, TARGET_DEPTH - depth)\n            f = call(api.step_down, step)\n            depth += step\n            if f > JAM_N:\n                # Jammed: back off, then pull completely out and give up on this candidate.\n                call(api.step_down, -(depth + HOVER * 1000.0))\n                return False\n        if call(api.done):\n            return True\n        # Not reported seated: push slightly further once.\n        if left() >= 2:\n            f = call(api.step_down, 2.0)\n            if f <= JAM_N and call(api.done):\n                return True\n        return False\n\n    for dx, dy, dyaw in cands:\n        # need: move + probe + retract, or move + probe + ~9 insertion steps + done\n        if left() < 14:\n            break\n        if try_insert(hx + dx, hy + dy, hyaw + dyaw):\n            return\n    return\n",
